program	errors/two_exclusive_only_windows_conflict.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	differs
expect	error
build	refused	exclusive access violation: the place `b.tally(…)` borrows `b` EXCLUSIVELY even though this window only reads — `Bag.tally` mutates `self` outside the place it lends (a write into receiver storage at line 34) — and `b` is accessed by reference a second time in the same call
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: exclusive access violation: the place `b.tally(…)` borrows `b` EXCLUSIVELY even though this window only reads — `Bag.tally` mutates `self` outside the place it lends (a write into receiver storage at line 34) — and `b` is accessed by reference a second time in the same call"
log	"  --> examples/errors/two_exclusive_only_windows_conflict.saw:42:18"
log	"     |"
log	" 42 |     print(\"{pair(&b.tally(0), &b.tally(1))}\")"
log	"     |                  ^"
log	"   hint: a read-only RESULT is not a shared receiver BORROW: an accessor whose body mutates the receiver takes it exclusively at every use site, so this is the same conflict two `&var` windows would be. Open the accesses in SEPARATE statements, or move the bookkeeping behind `#lend_var` so the shared specialization does not need an exclusive receiver"
log	""
log	"1 error(s) generated"
